# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two FILES, never a
# shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is defined in run_gates.sh.
# Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_extractor_unity.py" "UNITY EXTRACTOR GATE: PASS" "Unity / C# minimal-credible extractor coverage: hand-edited Unity asset family yields file nodes (no 'Unknown' verdict), engine cache trees pruned, C# still parses" "Unity asset extractor: .meta / .unity / .prefab / .asset / .asmdef / .asmref / .shader / .cginc / .hlsl / .compute added to _SOURCE_EXT so build_graph emits a bare file node (language='unity') for every hand-authored Unity asset. WITHOUT this, a Unity PR (example-org/game-app dogfood) hit core.main_impact_surface's 'paths not in main's graph' branch on every scene/prefab edit -> 'Veripsa - Unknown' verdict. Content-free: no structural edges from YAML (conservative bias keeps prefab GUIDs / scene-object references out of the moat; they would noise-couple). Cache prune: Library/ + Temp/ + MemoryCaptures/ added to _SKIP_DIRS (the standard Unity .gitignore tree) so engine-generated artifacts never reach the graph. .cs continues through the regular tree-sitter-c-sharp path (no behavior change on existing C# repos). BEFORE: a PR that only touched Assets/Scenes/Main.unity yielded zero file nodes for that path -> 'Unknown'. AFTER: each scene/prefab/.meta is a file node so the verdict graduates to a real (no-impact / direct-collision) outcome." "Unity extractor gate: synthetic Unity layout (Assets/Scripts/PlayerController.cs + .cs.meta, Assets/Scenes/Main.unity + .meta, Assets/Prefabs/Bullet.prefab, Assets/Data/Settings.asset, Assets/Game.Player.asmdef, Assets/Shaders/Simple.shader; Library/ + Temp/ + MemoryCaptures/ as engine cache). Asserts: every hand-authored Unity asset surfaces as a file node with language='unity'; .cs still parses (or degrades to a noded csharp file if the grammar is absent); Library/Temp/MemoryCaptures contents are PRUNED; scene yields NO structural edges (content-free)." 16
